From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: pinetab2: keep vdd_cpu flat across the CPU OPPs

The PineTab 2 resets - a silent power-on reset, nothing in the kernel log,
CRU reset status clear, PMIC on/off-source unchanged - whenever cpufreq
changes the CPU voltage while the cores are under heavy NEON load;
libcamera's software ISP triggers it within a handful of five-frame capture
cycles under schedutil. The same load runs indefinitely with the frequency
pinned.

Everything around the voltage write was tried and made no difference:
a settling margin after the write, forced PWM mode on the regulator, i2c0
at 100 kHz, the slowest and the fastest slew, a register cache so the hot
path is a single write, and a table whose steps are one 6.25 mV LSB. Heavy
read traffic to the regulator and to the PMIC under the same load is fine.
A voltage-flat table - no VSEL write at all - survives every test. So the
TCS4525 on this board does not tolerate a voltage-change command under
load, and the fix is not to issue one: run every OPP at the 1.8 GHz
voltage. It costs some idle power; it keeps the tablet up.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3566-pinetab2.dtsi
@@ -280,6 +280,34 @@
 &cpu3 {
 	cpu-supply = <&vdd_cpu>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Run every CPU OPP at the 1.8 GHz voltage. The TCS4525 feeding the cores
+ * cannot take a voltage-change command while the cores are loaded: the
+ * tablet power-cycles within a few DVFS steps under NEON-heavy work
+ * (libcamera's software ISP is the reliable trigger). Frequency changes
+ * without a voltage write are fine, so keep vdd_cpu flat.
+ */
+&cpu0_opp_table {
+	opp-408000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-600000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-816000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1104000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1416000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+	opp-1608000000 {
+		opp-microvolt = <1150000 1150000 1150000>;
+	};
+};
 
 &cru {
 	assigned-clocks = <&pmucru CLK_RTC_32K>, <&cru PLL_GPLL>,
